Z||000000||Gold87SE||11-28-2000||02:14 AM||||What's the proper way to burp a Fiero?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-28-2000||02:43 AM||||Lightly pat it on the roof just behind the sunroof.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||11
Z||000002||Oreif||11-28-2000||02:48 AM||||The easiest way is to park on an incline, rear side higher than front. (or raise the back of the car) Remove cap from thermostat, Then CAREFULLY remove the radiator cap in front. If you can remove it without coolant spilling you are way low on coolant. Just loosen it enough to let any air out (you will spill coolant)and then tighten it. Once that is done fill from back until it is full. Start engine let it run a few seconds then top off. Insert thermostat and cap it. If system is empty fill from back until front is over flowing. <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
